---
import FocusedOfferLayout from '../layouts/FocusedOfferLayout.astro';
import ExampleFinding from '../components/ExampleFinding.astro';
import type { Faq } from '../lib/schema';
const faq: Faq[] = [
  { q: 'What does a migration review cover?', a: 'The SQL the migration runs, the lock each statement takes and for how long, transaction boundaries, backfill batching, index builds, constraint validation, rollback, and whether old application versions still work during the rollout.' },
  { q: 'Can you tell which statements will block reads or writes?', a: 'Yes. For example, ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN with a volatile default rewrites the table under ACCESS EXCLUSIVE. Adding a foreign key takes SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE on both tables; adding it NOT VALID and running VALIDATE CONSTRAINT later avoids a long block.' },
  { q: 'Which migration tools do you review?', a: 'Any tool that produces SQL, including Rails, Django, Alembic, Prisma, Flyway and Liquibase. Send the generated SQL, because the lock behaviour depends on what actually runs.' },
  { q: 'Do you need access to my repository?', a: 'No. Send a sanitized summary first, then the bounded patch or generated SQL through an agreed channel. Repository access and production credentials are not needed for scoping.' },
  { q: 'Do you review SQL Server stored procedures too?', a: 'Yes, though this page focuses on PostgreSQL. For SQL Server, I check the engine version and edition before recommending an index or online operation.' }
];
---
<FocusedOfferLayout service="database-code-review" title="PostgreSQL Schema & Migration Code Review | WalStack" eyebrow="Database Code Review · one change" heading="PostgreSQL schema and migration code review" faq={faq}
  description="Independent review of one PostgreSQL schema change, migration or database pull request: severity-ranked findings, lock and rollout risks, validation checks."
  headline="Find database performance and migration risks before they reach production."
  fit="For engineering leads and agencies shipping a database-heavy feature. Choose one pull request or migration whose correctness, locking behavior or rollout sequence needs a second reading."
  excludes="Application security audits, infrastructure reviews, unlimited PR reviews and production implementation require a different scope. Static review cannot establish how every change will behave under load.">
  <Fragment slot="inputs"><p>Use a sanitized change summary in the enquiry. Include engine/version, approximate affected rows, deployment order and which old application versions may still be running.</p>
    <p>After agreement, share the bounded patch or generated SQL through the agreed channel. Repository access and production credentials are unnecessary for initial scoping.</p></Fragment>
  <p slot="result">Each finding points to the relevant statement, explains the correctness or performance risk, and identifies a test or evidence gap before release.</p>
  <p>This review reads a change before it ships. If a database change has already slowed production PostgreSQL, the <a href="/snapshot">free snapshot</a> or a <a href="/postgresql-performance-investigation">slowdown investigation</a> fits better.</p>
  <h2>Example finding</h2>
  <ExampleFinding label="From a measured lab on generated data. Not a client incident."
    symptom="Shortly after a deploy started, a busy endpoint stopped responding. Reader throughput fell to zero for about 14 seconds, while query plans stayed healthy."
    cause="A catalog-only ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN note text needed ACCESS EXCLUSIVE and queued behind a session left idle in transaction. Every later read on orders queued behind the waiting ALTER."
    fix={`SET lock_timeout = '2s';  -- migration session only
ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN note text;
-- on timeout: retry later, with a backoff`}
    lockRisk="With the timeout, the ALTER gave up after 2.01 seconds and readers recovered. The migration still has to be retried, and the idle-in-transaction session is the real fix."
    validation="pg_blocking_pids() shows no queue behind the migration session, and endpoint latency stays flat during the deploy."
    source={{ href: '/case-studies/lab-lock-queue', label: 'The full lock-queue lab' }} />
  <h2>Questions the patch should answer</h2>
  <h3>Which statements and plans change?</h3><p>I review queries, stored procedures, functions and database-related ORM changes alongside the data-access patterns they serve. An index addition can speed a read and add write cost. An index removal needs evidence over a representative workload window.</p>
  <h3>Who waits during rollout?</h3><p>For schema migrations (<code>ALTER TABLE</code>, new constraints, new indexes) and backfills I trace transaction boundaries, lock duration, retry behavior and rollback options. PostgreSQL concurrent index builds and SQL Server index operations have different restrictions. I check the engine version and, for SQL Server, edition before recommending a strategy. See the <a href="/insights/postgresql-create-index-concurrently-stuck">concurrent index build guide</a> for a PostgreSQL example.</p>
  <h3>When does a review need production evidence?</h3><p>If the decision depends on actual wait time, parameter distribution or competing writers, the report names the missing observation. For a wider incident, request a separate <a href="/postgresql-performance-investigation">PostgreSQL investigation</a> or <a href="/sql-server-performance">SQL Server performance review</a>.</p>
</FocusedOfferLayout>
